#28: 
> On Sat, Jul 30, 2016 at 7:23 AM, Michael Ellerman <mpe@ellerman.id.au> wrote:

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc_node(sizeof(*crng)...) over kmalloc_node(sizeof(struct crng_state)...)
#99: FILE: drivers/char/random.c:1674:
+		crng = kmalloc_node(sizeof(struct crng_state), GFP_KERNEL, i);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

